use miden::standards::wallets::basic as basic_wallet

#! FEE script: moves the assets carried by the note into the consuming account's vault.
#!
#! The script performs no target check and no sender check, so the note can be consumed by any
#! account exposing `receive_asset`. It is essentially a P2ID note without the target account check.
#!
#! This is how a transaction pays its fee to a batch builder: whichever account builds the batch
#! consumes the note during batch construction. Because the note is payable to nobody in particular,
#! the payer does not need to know who the builder will be.
#!
#! WARNING: this note pays whoever consumes it first, so it cannot be used to pay a specific party.
#!
#! Requires that the account exposes:
#! - miden::standards::wallets::basic::receive_asset procedure.
#!
#! Inputs:  [ARGS, pad(12)]
#! Outputs: [pad(16)]
#!
#! Where:
#! - ARGS are the note arguments, which this script ignores.
#!
#! Panics if:
#! - Account does not expose miden::standards::wallets::basic::receive_asset procedure.
#! - The same non-fungible asset already exists in the account.
#! - Adding a fungible asset would result in amount overflow, i.e., the total amount would be
#!   greater than 2^63.
@note_script
pub proc main
    dropw
    # => [pad(16)]

    exec.basic_wallet::add_assets_to_account
    # => [pad(16)]
end
